From: fenleon <fenleon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:43:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] voip: reply to peer re-ICE with relay rebuild (1:1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A mid-call network switch made the peer re-ICE
(<transport transport-message-type="3">); we ignored it and the peer
gave up ~5s later, with our video degraded permanently — our own relay
socket had died with the old network and nothing rebuilt it.

The handler now answers an active 1:1 call's re-ICE with the type-9
transport reply (build_transport) and pokes the media engine through
the video-control plumbing (VideoControl::RebuildRelay ->
eng.rebuild_relay), which mirrors the group relay-refresh tail of
commit_group_allocate: retire the transport, redial the stored relay
endpoint, re-allocate on the same credentials, arm the response budget
in relay_reconnected. The driver's existing ReconnectRelay arm does the
redial, so no watchdog or per-packet logging — one-shot INFO markers
only (battery rule).
